{
  "analysis": "The change adds JSONField-specific rendering and may fix ordinary dictionary values, but uses database preparation instead of form-field preparation and does not handle InvalidJSONInput or serialization failures safely. The added scripts are development artifacts rather than integrated regression tests, and the execution check provides no test evidence.",
  "scores": {"R1": 2, "R2": 2, "R3": 2, "R4": 2, "R5": 1, "R6": 2, "R7": 2},
  "reasons": {
    "R1": "The ordinary dictionary case is addressed, but the explicitly requested InvalidJSONInput-aware preparation is missing.",
    "R2": "Calling model-field get_prep_value() without fallback can raise serialization errors and does not preserve InvalidJSONInput behavior.",
    "R3": "Three standalone debugging scripts are unnecessary additions to a narrowly scoped admin display fix.",
    "R4": "The patch bypasses form-field display preparation, adds an out-of-order import instead of using models.JSONField, and places tests outside the established suite.",
    "R5": "The execution check found no runnable tests, so there is no demonstrated regression coverage.",
    "R6": "The small production branch is understandable, but repetitive print-heavy scripts, hard-coded paths, and unused imports substantially reduce clarity.",
    "R7": "Use appropriate form-field preparation with safe fallback, remove debugging artifacts, and add integrated regression tests before merging."
  }
}

{
  "analysis": "Removing the __file__ check enables namespace-package discovery, but the additional migration-count condition incorrectly reclassifies ordinary empty migrations packages as unmigrated. The new test references a fixture absent from the diff, and the execution check reports failure with the patch applied.",
  "scores": {"R1": 3, "R2": 2, "R3": 3, "R4": 3, "R5": 1, "R6": 4, "R7": 2},
  "reasons": {
    "R1": "The patch enables namespace discovery but changes empty-package semantics beyond the requested removal of the obsolete __file__ restriction.",
    "R2": "Classifying every package without migration files as unmigrated regresses ordinary empty migrations packages and can alter syncdb behavior.",
    "R3": "The migration-count-based classification is an unnecessary behavioral change beyond accepting namespace packages.",
    "R4": "The patch retains existing discovery patterns but departs from the loader's established distinction between an empty migrations package and an unmigrated app.",
    "R5": "The added test references a namespace fixture not supplied in the diff, and the execution check confirms that tests fail with the patch applied.",
    "R6": "The code is straightforward, although the new classification comment explains an unnecessary policy change.",
    "R7": "Restore empty-package behavior and provide a working namespace-package fixture and passing regression tests before merging."
  }
}

{
  "analysis": "The adapter change attempts to preserve stored coordinate dtypes and honor explicit NumPy dtype requests, but the shared index-construction change also forces every input dtype through pandas. That introduces compatibility risks for dtypes pandas cannot use as index dtypes, without demonstrating that stacking preserves the original dtype end to end. No regression tests were added.",
  "scores": {"R1": 3, "R2": 2, "R3": 3, "R4": 3, "R5": 1, "R6": 3, "R7": 2},
  "reasons": {
    "R1": "The adapter conversion targets the reported symptom, but preserving int32 through MultiIndex creation is not established by the patch.",
    "R2": "Passing arbitrary array dtypes explicitly to pd.Index can reject otherwise valid inputs, such as float16 arrays on pandas versions that only support wider numeric indexes.",
    "R3": "Changing shared index construction for all non-object dtypes broadens the impact beyond the stacking-specific conversion.",
    "R4": "The change uses existing APIs but bypasses the deliberate distinction between pandas index storage and xarray coordinate dtype metadata.",
    "R5": "No tests were added to reproduce the int32 stacking bug or check compatibility with other coordinate dtypes.",
    "R6": "The adapter branch contains redundant result assignments and comments that largely restate the code.",
    "R7": "The broad dtype-construction change needs revision and regression coverage before merging."
  }
}
